# Git guesses whether a file is binary by sniffing its first 8000 bytes, and it gets
# the book's PDF wrong — nothing in that window contains a NUL, so `git diff` counted
# 47,975 lines of PDF text for the commit that added it, and `git grep` can even match
# strings inside the file. Naming the types outright prevents both, and more importantly
# stops Git text-merging a replaced book: a conflicted PDF would come out with `>>>>>>>`
# markers embedded in it, i.e. a file that no longer opens.

*.pdf  binary
*.epub binary

# Same reason for the images: vlog thumbnails and Weibo images are regenerated in bulk
# by scripts, so a merge touching the same screenshot is a real scenario, and they are
# small enough that a text diff of one is pure noise.

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary